.SH "NAME"
lxsession \- lightweight X session manager
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBlxsession\fR\ 'u
\fBlxsession\fR [\fB\fIOPTIONS\fR\fR...]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBlxsession\fR
is a program that provides an X session manager\&. It is the default X session manager for LXDE\&.
.PP
A session manager automatically starts a set of applications and sets up a working desktop environment\&. Additionally, when a user logs out, the session manager remembers which applications were in use and restarts them the next time the user logs in\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-noautostart\fR
.RS 4
disable autostart of applications (window\-manager mode only)
.RE
.PP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-compatibility \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR
.RS 4
specify a compatibility mode for settings (only
\fIrazor\-qt\fR
is supported)
.RE
.PP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-de \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR
.RS 4
name of the desktop environnement (\fILXDE\fR
is the default)
.RE
.PP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-noxsettings\fR
.RS 4
disable Xsettings daemon support
.RE
.PP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-reload\fR
.RS 4
reload configurations (for Xsettings daemon)
.RE
.PP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR
.RS 4
name of the desktop session profile
.RE
